# .gitignore used as a WHITELIST
# 1. Block everything by default with an all-encompassing wildcard *
*

# 2. A second line is needed because of the way Git handles files: 
# if it sees a directory is blocked, it won't even try to check 
# anything in the directory to see if it was unblocked later. 
# It simply skips it and ignores all rules inside that directory. 
# So, !*/ here tells Git to specifically check subfolders.
!*/

# track these files
!.gitignore
!index.html
!LICENSE
!README.md
    
# whitelist everything in ./samples/
!samples/